WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.539
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 5: On the Farm.

2
00:00:03.619 --> 00:00:06.781
In this unit you will learn about the farm.

3
00:00:06.861 --> 00:00:14.546
You will name the farm animals and the sounds they
make, learn farm words like tractor, barn and field,

4
00:00:14.626 --> 00:00:20.276
and talk about the work people do on
a farm — feeding, planting and picking.

5
00:00:20.356 --> 00:00:26.458
You will see how animals and plants grow:
a chick from an egg, a bean from a seed.

6
00:00:26.538 --> 00:00:30.982
You will hear a gentle story about helping and working hard.

7
00:00:31.062 --> 00:00:37.466
Say the words out loud — this is about
speaking with confidence, not perfect spelling.

8
00:00:37.546 --> 00:00:43.799
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:43.879 --> 00:00:52.248
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name common
farm animals (cow, hen, chick, duck, sheep, goat, horse…)

10
00:00:52.328 --> 00:00:57.511
You will also say the sound each
animal makes (moo, cluck, quack, baa…)

11
00:00:57.591 --> 00:01:03.588
You will also name farm places and things
(farm, barn, field, tractor, egg, seed).

12
00:01:03.668 --> 00:01:06.331
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:06.411 --> 00:01:11.554
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: cow, hen, chick, duck, goose, pig.

14
00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:16.843
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:16.923 --> 00:01:20.957
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:21.037 --> 00:01:25.991
The reading sequence includes Amal and
the Little Hen and Talk about On the Farm.

17
00:01:26.071 --> 00:01:26.861
Read actively.

18
00:01:26.941 --> 00:01:31.149
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:31.229 --> 00:01:35.188
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:35.268 --> 00:01:38.484
The first language focus is Name a farm animal.

21
00:01:38.564 --> 00:01:39.957
Name one farm animal.

22
00:01:40.037 --> 00:01:44.937
Say 'a' before most words, but 'an'
before a vowel sound: a cow, an ox.

23
00:01:45.017 --> 00:01:52.581
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:01:52.661 --> 00:01:56.531
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

25
00:01:56.611 --> 00:02:00.869
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:00.949 --> 00:02:04.171
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:04.251 --> 00:02:07.603
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:07.683 --> 00:02:09.156
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:09.236 --> 00:02:15.841
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:15.921 --> 00:02:19.082
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:19.162 --> 00:02:26.577
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
